This chapter specifies how the parts of the Morloc ecosystem fit together:
the compiler, the runtime library, the nexus, and the environment manager. It
defines where each part is installed, how a program's dependencies (Morloc
modules and foreign packages) are resolved and locked, how an environment is
frozen into a portable artifact, and how a compiled program is served to other
programs and agents. The <<apis>> chapter shows how to use these tools; this
chapter specifies what they do.

This chapter and the two that follow are written as a specification. They
describe behavior, formats and guarantees rather than any particular
implementation, so they should remain true of any conforming reimplementation.

